  "headline": "Tamil Nadu Police Detain BJP Leaders During Karthigai Deepam Event",
  "seoTitle": "Tamil Nadu BJP Leaders Detained During Karthigai Deepam",
  "metaDescription": "Tamil Nadu police detained BJP leaders and imposed restrictions in Madurai as the state prepares for the Karthigai Deepam ceremony at Thirupparankundram.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Tamil Nadu authorities detained the state BJP president and several other political figures amidst ongoing tensions surrounding the Karthigai Deepam festival.",
    "Madurai district officials implemented prohibitory orders under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, restricting public access to Thirupparankundram hill.",
    "Following a Supreme Court directive, a ceremonial lamp is scheduled to be lit on the hill, though access is strictly limited to authorized personnel."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Tensions have escalated in Madurai, Tamil Nadu, as the district administration prepares for the annual Karthigai Deepam festival. Local police have deployed thousands of officers and erected barricades around Thirupparankundram hill to enforce security measures. Prohibitory orders under Section 163 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita are currently in effect across the district. In response to the high-security environment, several leaders from the Bharatiya Janata Party, including the state president, have been placed under house arrest or detained by police while attempting to visit the site. The security operations follow a Supreme Court order that permits a one-time ceremonial lighting of a lamp at the hilltop temple. Simultaneously, Karnataka has approached the Supreme Court regarding a separate infrastructure dispute involving the Cauvery–South Vellar–Vaigai–Gundar Link Project, questioning the legitimacy of work initiated by the Tamil Nadu government.",
